WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.520
In cinema, a little allure goes a long way.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:09.040
When it comes to unintentional wardrobe malfunctions,
however, the effect can be more humorous than

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.040
titillating.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.590
We're here to show you a handful of our favorite
wardrobe flubs.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:18.130
There's something special about the Star Wars
film universe's far-reaching, wide-ranging

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.130
appeal.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.380
Though creator George Lucas reportedly owned
up to purposely making his prequel installments

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:29.029
more friendly to a younger audience, a vast
majority of Star Wars fanatics are adults.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.280
And apart from an innuendo or two likely meant
to make the older crowd chuckle, the movies

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.600
have remained largely squeaky clean -- with
one notable exception.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.200
In Return of the Jedi, actress Femi Taylor
portrays Oola, the green-skinned slave dancer

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.950
Jabba the Hutt holds captive in his palace.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.240
Before Oola meets her grisly death at the
mouth of a hungry Rancor, Jabba makes her

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.560
strut about in her skimpy outfit while he
watches.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.680
When he grabs hold of Oola's chain during
the sequence, he causes a wardrobe malfunction

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.010
that makes her costume reveal something you'd
never think you'd see in a Star Wars movie.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.470
The slip happens in the blink of an eye, but
it definitely ended up in the movie.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:10.630
The fact that Lucas was a stickler for scrubbing
up footage for home releases makes it especially

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.210
bizarre that this malfunction didn't end up
on the cutting room floor.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.950
Watchers of Vanilla Sky aren't left wanting
additional adrenaline-pumping action, an extra

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:25.240
smattering of stirring sci-fi, or more eyebrow-raising
decisions that make Tom Cruise's character

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.090
seem genuinely dangerous.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:31.649
One of the most noteworthy scenes in the film
involves such a move made by Cruise's David

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:36.549
Aames, who captures Cameron Diaz's Julianna
Gianni, his one-time lover, and straps her

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:37.549
to the bed.

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:42.030
Diaz, wearing a sheer dress, attempts to flip
herself over on the mattress, and in doing

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:45.350
so, accidentally shifts the top of the garment
out of place.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.969
The actress is quick to fix the wardrobe malfunction
mid-scene, pulling the gown into its original

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:54.070
position, but the chest-exposing take wound
up in the film's final cut.

00:01:55.259 --> 00:01:59.740
Arnold Schwarzenegger has been in the spotlight
since his days as one of the world's foremost

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.389
champion bodybuilders.

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:06.009
Over the years, he has starred in a plethora
of blockbuster action flicks and, of course,

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:07.689
governed the state of California.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:12.860
But even the former "Governator" has suffered
an incident on the set, experiencing a wardrobe

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.610
malfunction countless fans have noticed.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.850
During the opening scene of 1984's The Terminator,
Arnold Schwarzenegger walks around in his

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.480
birthday suit before he gets the chance to
cover up.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.561
Low lighting, clever distant camera angles,
and the stereotypically poor quality of the

00:02:27.561 --> 00:02:32.700
original 1980s footage preserve Schwarzenegger's
dignity for the most part, but those naughty

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.060
bits still made it into the movie — the
remastered Blu-ray edition shows the actor

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:42.160
stark naked and on full display as he approaches
a group of young ruffians.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.910
"I think this guy's a couple cans short of
a six pack."

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.410
"You're clothes.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.410
Give them to me."

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:55.360
In the 1980s, VHS cassettes were the state-of-the-art
form of media distribution, and without an

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.560
internet, salacious rumors and news about
movies spread via word of mouth.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.410
These are the factors that spread the notion
that there is a moment of accidental near

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.650
nudity in the 1985 horror comedy Teen Wolf.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:11.380
Pause the tape at just the right moment, the
rumor said, and viewers would see an extra

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:15.660
in a crowd shot with the fly of their pants
wide open, and the white underwear beneath

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:16.780
fully visible.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.860
The scene in question is a high school basketball
game in which the titular teen wolf Scott

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.710
Howard aggressively competes.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:26.920
The crowd cheers, and a shot of a spectator
in the grandstands made it into the final

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.800
cut of the film, and the zipper of their pants
is indeed unzipped.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:36.120
This definitely isn't the most graphic example
on this list, but it's nonetheless a solid

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.291
example of a surprising editing mistake.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:45.170
Considering that Samuel L. Jackson has previously
expressed his view that nude scenes are, quote,

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:49.290
"extremely awkward" to film, you'd be right
to assume that the prolific actor has never

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.230
in his decades-long career sauntered around
in his birthday suit for a movie.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.480
As it happens, however, you'd be wrong.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.540
In the 2001 drama pic The Caveman's Valentine,
Jackson plays a paranoid schizophrenic man

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.920
who becomes inextricably involved in a murder
mystery.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.430
At one point, he strips down and struts past
a mirror in a scene likely meant to show off

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.600
only his buttocks.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.740
But, as most malfunctions go, a lot more was
caught on camera.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.880
In a flashbulb moment while his backside is
on display, viewers can see Jackson's frontside,

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.880
too.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.630
The Caveman's Valentine never got a Blu-ray
release, meaning no one will ever see a high-resolution

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:30.460
shot of Jackson's nether region, so his dignity
is at least partly preserved.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:36.150
The 1981 Australian drama war film Gallipoli
is noteworthy for a few reasons: It took home

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:41.850
a grand total of eight Australian Film Institute
awards, boomed in the box office down under,

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:46.240
earned a Golden Globe nomination for Best
Foreign Film in 1982, and fared well with

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.240
critics.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.580
It's also become known for a vastly different
reason: Gallipoli features a bit more of Mel

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:52.810
Gibson.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.880
A then-25-year-old Gibson shows off everything
he's got during a scene in which his character

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:01.920
— Archy Hamilton, the stockman and sprinter
with his sights set on the Australian Imperial

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.580
Force — sheds his colors to go for a swim
with his soldier pals.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.540
When he dives down to the seafloor, we end
up seeing more of Gibson than we should have.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:14.860
He clearly wasn't given any costume modifications
to help prevent any slippage, and the shot

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:18.770
wasn't clipped out of the theatrical or home
release versions of the film.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:25.210
Bad Boys II is a small slice of heaven for
any fan of the buddy cop and action-comedy

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.210
genres.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.460
It's got a leading duo who work off one another's
attitudes and push each other's buttons; a

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.990
high-stakes mission the pair have to embark
on; a seemingly indomitable villain; and the

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:40.770
ubiquitous beautiful and badass woman who
ends up a love interest for one of the protagonists.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:45.080
Gabrielle Union is that more-than-a-pretty-face
character in the film, so it's unsurprising

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.680
that she's seen sporting some revealing outfits.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.860
One in particular is a little too low-cut,
however.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.360
In a scene where Union's character chucks
a gun toward a live minefield and then ducks

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.990
for cover, her cut-out dress slides sideways
to reveal her nipple.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.510
In real time, the malfunction is a bit hard
to spot, but slow down the footage just a

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:05.190
tad, and you'll see Union's chest clear as
day.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:11.430
Denzel Washington leads the 1991 crime thriller
Ricochet, playing LAPD Detective-Lieutenant

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:14.370
and Assistant District Attorney Nicholas Styles.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.910
During a locker room scene, an unclothed Washington
leaps up from the bench to hide behind a locker

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.060
door when a woman enters the men-only zone.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.250
In this split moment, his manhood gets a fraction
of a second of fame.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:30.300
An untrained eye wouldn't be able to zero
in on the explicit shot, but if you look just

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.780
carefully enough, it's definitely there.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:39.770
There Will Be Blood is the story of a greed-driven
oil man named Daniel Plainview, fascinatingly

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.990
portrayed with shocking brutality by Daniel
Day-Lewis.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:47.670
The actor received his second of three Best
Actor Academy Awards for his work as a driving

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:52.729
force of the California oil boom in the late
1800s and early 1900s.

00:06:52.729 --> 00:06:57.800
Plainview aggressively cajoles and bends rivals
and allies alike to his will, traipsing all

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.710
over others metaphorically when he's not traipsing
literally around his land holdings dotted

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.210
with big, noisy oil derricks.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:10.960
Such labor requires a solid, reliable, and
sturdy pair of work boots, and Plainview can

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.550
be seen wearing a pair of brown leather ones.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:17.740
They look suitably expensive, but they also
look unsuitably modern.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:21.570
During a moment of rest, the camera shows
the bottom of Plainview's boots, and they

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:25.450
bear a waffle pattern, the kind found on early
Nike running shoes.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:30.290
The latter is widely acknowledged as the originator
of that kind of groove — which it pioneered

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:34.199
in 1972, decades after the California oil
boom.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:41.490
Dazed and Confused is one of the best teen
movies of all time, a personal and casually

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:45.060
realistic look at the night after the last
day of school in 1976.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:50.290
Not a whole lot happens, just like what happens
when real kids get together, both then and

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.290
now.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.650
Early in the film, various characters cruise
around town in their cars.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:58.470
During a scene shot from the point of view
of one of these teens as they navigate traffic,

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:03.120
a motorcyclist can be seen wearing a vest-type
jacket adorned with the skull logo used by

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.140
the punk band The Misfits.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:10.580
Though this skull drawing can be traced back
to the 1930s, it's still likely an anachronism.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:15.950
Dazed and Confused takes place in 1976, a
year before the band formed, and five years

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.020
before it publicly unveiled the skull logo.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.970
Pulp Fiction, possibly Quentin Tarantino's
most beloved film, thoroughly earns the R

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:28.690
rating bestowed upon it by the Motion Picture
Association of America.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:34.880
The F-word is uttered more than 260 times,
a character suffers a near fatal drug overdose,

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.970
and grisly violence is scattered throughout.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.419
"What country are you from?"

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:39.419
"What?"

00:08:39.419 --> 00:08:41.020
"What ain't no country I ever heard of.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.469
They speak English in 'What'?"

00:08:42.469 --> 00:08:48.000
Despite all that tawdry stuff, there's only
one bit of nudity, and it was seemingly accidental.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.100
During a quiet moment when Butch hides out
with his girlfriend Fabienne after refusing

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:54.460
to throw a boxing match, he takes a shower.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:58.500
When he gets out, he grabs a towel while Fabienne
brushes her teeth, but Willis doesn't hold

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.110
the fabric high enough, thus revealing his
manhood to moviegoers.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:06.100
Later, when Pulp Fiction aired on television,
the towel was digitally stretched to cover

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.790
the uncovered parts of Butch.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:14.600
The works of 19th century English author Jane
Austen enjoyed a surge of popularity in the

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.630
1990s.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:22.070
Arguably the most successful '90s Austen-based
project was 1995's Sense and Sensibility,

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:27.080
which won cast member Emma Thompson a screenwriting
Oscar and elevated the outside-the-U.K. fame

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.750
of her co-stars Kate Winslet and Hugh Laurie.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:35.980
The intricately realized film also has a few
modern touches, although one was clearly unintentional:

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:39.660
With Colonel Brandon looking on, Mr. Palmer
reluctantly holds an infant.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.260
The baby's outerwear is Regency-appropriate,
but its other garments are not.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:48.860
The little one wears a 20th century-style
disposable diaper, which certainly wasn't

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:51.600
available in 1810.

